# Test: a peer block that names its AS opens with that AS in BOTH carriers
# RFC 6793 defines, and the eBGP session establishes.
#
# VALIDATES: option=asn:value=N reaches the My Autonomous System field AND the
#            Capability Value of capability 65 (buildOpen, internal/test/peer/open.go).
#            Ze reads the capability first, as RFC 6793 Section 4.1 requires
#            (openAdvertisedAS, internal/component/bgp/reactor/peer.go), and
#            accepts the session because that AS is the one this peer is
#            configured for (validateOpenPeerAS,
#            internal/component/bgp/reactor/session_open_as.go).
# PREVENTS:  the two carriers disagreeing. ze-peer used to copy ze's OPEN and
#            overwrite the two-octet field alone, so the mirrored capability 65
#            still carried ZE's AS and ze answered NOTIFICATION 2/2 Bad Peer AS.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: ze is AS 65533 and the peer is AS 65010, so the two carriers
# cannot agree by accident. With capability 65 left at ze's AS, ze reads 65533
# from a peer configured for 65010, answers OPEN Message Error / Bad Peer AS, and
# neither the UPDATE below nor the End-of-RIB after it ever arrives.

# ze-peer expectations
stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
option=asn:value=65010
cmd=api:conn=1:seq=1:text=send bgp * update text origin igp as-path [65533] nhop 10.0.1.254 nlri ipv4/unicast add 10.0.0.0/24
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF002F02000000144001010040020602010000FFFD4003040A0001FE180A0000
expect=json:conn=1:seq=1:json={"meta":{"version":"1.0.0","format":"ze-bgp"},"message":{"type":"update"},"peer":{"address":"127.0.0.1","remote":{"as":65010}},"direction":"in","as-path":[65533],"origin":"igp","ipv4/unicast":[{"action":"add","nlri":["10.0.0.0/24"],"next-hop":"10.0.1.254"}]}
cmd=api:conn=1:seq=1:text=send bgp * update text nlri ipv4/unicast eor
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00170200000000
EOF_PEER

# ze bgp configuration
stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65533
				remote 65010
			}
			router-id 10.0.0.2
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
		}
		timer {
			receive-hold-time 180
		}

		update {
			attribute {
				origin igp
				next-hop 10.0.1.254
				local-preference 200
			}
			nlri {
				ipv4/unicast add 10.0.0.0/24
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

# Process orchestration
cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze-peer --port $PORT:stdin=peer
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=10s
